entity - typed data: host, user, standalone home. Produces nixosConfigurations etc appropriate to class.
den.hosts { <system>.<name> = {} }
den.homes
users live by host - den.hosts.<systems>.<host>.users.<name>

each host has a default aspect for configuring it den.aspects.<name>

Entities have different policy dispatch, classes have different module system evaluation.
Entities are instantiations of a schema e.g. `den.schema.host`
Entities may have options declared directly on the instance.
To apply to all instances of a schema `den.schema.host`, to apply to all instances globally, `den.schema.conf`.
You can make your own schemas and instantiate them.
Schemas get some stuff automatically, particularly context arguments pulled from the entities modules.

`den.policies` holds policies.
They're activated by being put in an `includes` list e.g. `den.schema.host.includes = [den.policies.<name>]`

core types can have arbitrary arguments passed, that are then available in aspects.
Disable with strict mode `imports = [ inputs.den.flakeModules.strict ];`

aspects can configure any of the core types in one, and can include other aspects.
